{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1542367-jiang-shi-unique-discipline-bloodlines-and-covenant","id":1542367,"title":"Jiang Shi Unique Discipline, Bloodlines, and Covenant","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-18T08:35:39-07:00","id":1542367,"title":"Jiang Shi Unique Discipline, Bloodlines, and Covenant","content":"I like the Jiang Shi, but it feel like they are there, they don't even have bloodline or unique discipline, even though they're a full clan that still exist within the modern night, so I'm here to change that, with a new Discipline that replace the Jiang Shi Celerity, 10 Bloodline, and a new Covenant for Vampire of Asia (Mostly South, Southeast, and East Asia).<br /> <br /> <b>Essence</b><br /> Jiang Shi need Essence to stay grounded within the land of the living, every time Jiang Shi wake up, he lose a point of Essence, unless he sleep in his grave. Jiang Shi can spend 1 Essence to inflict the (Numb) condition, or 3 Essence to inflict the (Addict) condition to the victim of their feeding.<br /> <br /> <b>Bane:</b> The Ephemeral Curse. Because their presence in<br /> this world is strangely light, they cannot cause either the<br /> Swooning or Scarred Conditions by feeding. And when the Jiang Shi have no Essence left, they suffer the (Languid) condition, until they have Essence in their system again.<br /> <br /> <b>Numb</b><br /> Suffer no wound penalties for the scene. Additionally, any rolls to detect by touch suffer -5 penalty.<br /> Possible Sources: Jiang Shi feeding on you<br /> Resolution: Wait a scene.\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Tempest God Body</b><br /> The wind blow, and death follow, this Discipline represent the Jiang Shi body connection to the wind and storm, but also to life and breath.<br /> <br /> <b>Extract Chi Flow</b><br /> The Jiang Shi, can steal more than just the blood out of living being, they can suck out the Essence within the blood. When Jiang Shi is feeding, he get one point of Essence for every 2 Lethal damage he deal, he can store Essence equal to his Resolve dot. If the Jiang Shi is feeding on animal, he gain Essence equal to Vitae he gain from it.<br /> <br /> <b>Great Leap Outward</b> \u25cf<br /> It is said that the Jiang Shi can leap up into the air with great ease. With the help of the wind, the Jiang Shi can jump and soar like a bird.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflextive<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One turn<br /> <b>Effect: </b>The Jiang Shi can jump 70 feet horizontally and 40 vertically, this distance increase every 35 feet for horizontal, and 20 feet for vertical, per dot in this Discipline, so with Tempest 4, Great Leap Outward can jump up to 140 feet horizontally, and 80 feet vertically. And they take no damage from the fall. While the Jiang Shi is in the air, they fall slowly, and move in the air, which make it look like they're flying, when this Discipline is still active, they fall at a rate of 1 feet per turn, and can move in the air, with speed equal to their Dexterity.<br /> <br /> <b>Stolen Breath</b> \u25cf\u25cf<br /> <b>Cost: </b>None<br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Strength + Brawl \u2013 Defense<br /> <b>Duration: </b>None<br /> <b>Effect: </b>Instead of bitting to suck the life out of mortal, Jiang Shi can choose to steal the breath of it victim, this isn't actual physical breath, but more of the victim animating life force. When feeding this way, the Jiang Shi gain Essence for every point of Lethal damage he deal, but gain no Vitae when feeding like this. If he is feeding from an animal, he gain Essence equal to it size.<br /> <br /> <b>Dust On The Wind</b> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Essence and 1 Vitae<br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Scene.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The Jiang Shi becomes insubstantial. The creature seems to turn into a cloud of dust or a noxious fume that quickly dissipates, but such merely masks the shift into Twilight, the insubstantial state shared by various ephemeral being. While in this state, the Jiang Shi may not utilize Vitae or any of his supernatural powers save for the various God Body Discipline and Chi Rite. He may, however, perceive and interact with ephemeral being. While in this state, the character\u2019s Speed becomes Strength + Dexterity + 10. Jiang Shi can steal Essence from ephemeral, when feeding Essence from an ephemeral being, the Jiang Shi don't deal any damage to it, instead he gain one Essence per turn, until the ephemeral leave the grapple, or it run out of Essence. The Jiang Shi can spend a Willpower to instantly teleport to it &quot;grave&quot; (the site where they become a Jiang Shi). The Jiang Shi can go between the frequency of the Twilight, and even go to the Shadow and the Underworld, but that would require another spending of 2 Essence.<br /> <br /> <b>Thunderbolt's Kiss \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</b><br /> A Jiang Shi using this power may hold lighting quietly and invisibly in her hand, waiting to be released or may cause it to arc and thunder about her hands and body. Depending<br /> upon the character's desires, she may appear to throw the<br /> lightning bolt at her foes, or it may simply jump from her hand (or eyes) and strike them, it have range of 40 yard per dot in Tempest God Body<br /> <b>Cost: </b>3 Essence<br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Tempest God Body + Occult + Dexterity<br /> <b>Duration: </b>1 Turn per Success<br /> <b>Roll Result<br /> Dramatic Failure: </b>The lighting go out of control and strike at the user instead, dealing 3 Lethal damage.<br /> <b>Failure: </b>Lighting can't manifest.<br /> <b>Success: </b>The lighting can deal 1 Lethal damage per success, and cause (Stunned) tilt.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>Same as regular Success, but cause (Immobilized) tilt instead.<br /> <br /> <b>The Flight of the Dragons</b> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> This most awesome of Tempest God Body powers allows a Jiang Shi to channel Chi through his body and into the world around<br /> him to affect the local weather patterns. Depending upon the amount of power he can muster, he can even cause terrible storm.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4 Essence and 3 Vitae<br /> <b>Action:</b> 1 Turn<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Tempest God Body + Occult + Dexterity<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Vary<br /> <b>Roll Result</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: </b>The body can't handle the amount of power channeling throughout it and the environment, suffer 3 Aggravated damage.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> Your power is only enough to have 1 type of environmental tilt, that affect 1 miles radius, and last for one scene.<br /> <b>Success: </b>You successfully change the environment, you can have 3 type of environmental tilt, that affect 4 miles radius, and last for 1 day per success.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> You can have 5 type of environmental tilt, that affect 16 miles radius, and last 1 week per success.<br /> <br /> <b>Chi Art</b><br /> The Jiang Shi also have instinctual knowledge of special Chi Art, a form mortal magic that they retain even in unlife, because of their unique Embrace. These Chi Art cost the same experiences as other Ritual Discipline. Library Merit affect Chi Art.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> one Essence or two Willpower per dot of Art, and each Art have it own special ingredient needed to cast the Rite.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Intelligence + Academic + Chi Art.<br /> <br /> Roll Result<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Gain (Wanton) Condition<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> Can apply (Sated) Condition if and when the ritual succeeds.<br /> <br /> <b>Heart Grave</b> \u25cf<br /> <b>Target of Success:</b> 2<br /> The Jiang Shi can relocate it &quot;grave&quot; (the location where it was Embrace) to another location, to do this they bury their heart in the location that they want to be their new grave, and then spill the Vitae of those pure of heart, mind, and soul. The Vitae the Jiang Shi require to spill is equal to 11 - their Humanity. Jiang Shi need their grave because, if they try to wake up outside of their grave, it take 2 Vitae instead of 1.<br /> <br /> <b>Eye of the Invisible</b> \u25cf\u25cf<br /> <b>Target of Success:</b> 3<br /> The Jiang Shi take out his eye from his socket, suffer 2 Lethal damage, and attune it to the Essence within his body, as he focusing on the type of being he wish to see. Once finished, he put his eye back on, and his sight can now detect trace and reveal the type of creature he focus on, this last until he go to sleep.\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Second Breath</b> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> <b>Target of Success: </b>4<br /> The Jiang Shi Embrace is different from the other Clan, their Embrace can only be done posthumous. They first need to drain the intended target of the Embrace of all their blood. Then they need to make a grave for them by digging out a hole for them, and spill the Vitae of those pure of heart, mind, and soul onto the target expose heart. The Jiang Shi need to spill a total of 10 Vitae into the target heart, and then bury the body, within the next 90 days, the corpse will rise from the grave and become a Jiang Shi, how long before the Jiang Shi rise depend on how powerful their Willpower is. The Jiang Shi can replace the target heart with the heart of the pure, which will give the Embrace Jiang Shi Blood Potency of 2 instead of 1.<br /> <br /> <b>Enlighten Mind</b> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> <b>Target of Success:</b> 5<br /> The Jiang Shi meditate on his nature, and what is existence thus far represent. At the end of his meditation, he gain a little spark of enlightenment, which clear his mind. The Jiang Shi get +5 to all roll that use Mental skill or attribute, this last for 24 hours, after which he mind is fog by madness and gain the (Madness) condition, and can't use this Art again until he resolve the condition.\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Mask of the Thousand Faces</b> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> <b>Target of Success: </b>6<br /> The Jiang Shi creates a mask and become the form of that mask. The Jiang Shi must kill the person he wish to assume form of, and use their skin as ingredient in making of the mask. The form created by this power typically possesses the same height, build, ethnicity, and gender of the victim, but otherwise the power can alter his appearance significantly. The Jiang Shi may choose to make the form particularly alluring, unassuming, or monsterous, granting a +3 bonus to Persuasion and Socialize (for the alluring), Stealth and Subterfuge (for the unassuming) or Intimidation and Brawl (for the monsterous). This power lasts for a month, though the Jiang Shi can end it as an instant action or extend it for another month with a recasting of this Art.<br /> <br /> <b>Devotion</b><br /> <br /> <b>Conjuring the Sidamen<br /> (Tempest God Body \u25cf\u25cf Animalism \u25cf)</b><br /> A Jiang Shi with this power has the ability to send out a call not a vocal call, but a sort of mental compulsion that summons to him a specific type of animal. The character may specify a desired species (tigers, birds-of-paradise, rhinos) or a more specific subject (Siberian tigers, alpha-male wolves). The animals summoned only come if they are within a two mile radius of the Jiang Shi location when he makes the call and if they are physically able to do so. This power does not grant control over animals, but those summoned by the call generally seem predisposed toward the Jiang Shi, and may fight for him if he appears to be in trouble. The animal that respond can spend Willpower of their own to be able to interact with ephemeral being for one turn for every Willpower spent.\u200b<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Vitae and 2 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Presence + Animal Ken + Tempest God Body<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant\u200b<br /> <b>Duration: </b>1 Scene<br /> <b>Roll Result<br /> Dramatic Failure:</b> No one answer you call.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> A single animal show up.<br /> <b>Success:</b> Half of the animals respond.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> All the animals responds, and you gain +3 to Animal Ken when trying to command them.<br /> <br /> This Devotion cost 3 Experience.<br /> <br /> <b>Unleash the Beast Spirit<br /> (Tempest God Body \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Animalism \u25cf\u25cf)</b><br /> This power creates such a great connection between the<br /> Jiang Shi and his own Beast, the Beast manifests itself in physical form. The Jiang Shi undergoes changes similar to those experienced by shapeshifters, becoming a sort of half-man, half-animal, with appropriate abilities.<br /> <b>Cost: </b>2 Vitae, 2 Essence, and 1 Willpower<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>None<br /> <b>\u200bAction: </b>3 Turn<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Scene<br /> <b>Effect: </b>The player must choose a &quot;totem animal&quot; which represent his Beast, for his character as soon as the character is able to use this power; the character's totem can never be changed. The Jiang Shi then changes into the form described above, which is similar to the wolf-man form of shapeshifter. The character receives 6 dots that he can use to increase his Attributes, as appropriate, to reflect this form. Additionally, his senses sharpen to reflect his animalistic nature, and at Storyteller's discretion he may gain other abilities based on his new form - for example, a Turtle totem might gain points of armor, a Shark totem improved swimming abilities and sharp teeth, and a Tiger totem claws.<br /> <br /> This Devotion cost 1 Experience.<br /> <br /> <b>The Hampering Smoke of Baigujing<br /> (Tempest God Body \u25cf\u25cf Obfuscate \u25cf)</b><br /> The Jiang Shi can cast smoke into the eye, temporary blinding people.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Vitae, 2 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Dexterity + Occult + Tempest Body<br /> <b>\u200bAction: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Scene<br /> <b>Effect: </b>The victim, who must be within 10 yards of the Jiang Shi when the power is used, will gain the (Blind) condition for one turn for every success achieved. And the victim suffer -3 to roll with Composure and Dexterity.<br /> <br /> This Devotion cost 3 Experience.<br /> <br /> <b>Storm Fist<br /> (Tempest God Body \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Obfuscate \u25cf\u25cf)</b><br /> The hand of the Jiang Shi turn blue and spark with energy.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Vitae, 3 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>None<br /> <b>\u200bAction:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration: </b>1 Scene<br /> <b>Effect: </b>One of the Jiang Shi hands glow bright blue as if it were made out of lighting. Fleshy object and creatur burst into flame when the hand touch them: consider this touch to be a Inferno fire with the intensity of +3. If they strikes or punches another character with their burning hand, they does their normal damage for that attack, and +3 dice of damage, all of which are considered to be aggravated.\u200b\u200b\u200b If a creature die of this power, their ash can be use as The Hampering Smoke of Baigujing.<br /> <br /> This Devotion cost 1 Experience.<br /> <br /> <b>Psychic Vampire</b><br /> Most Jiang Shi get Embrace by the Second Breath ritual, there are those whose Embrace are from no one. When a Psychic Vampire die, they usually stay dead, but if the Psychic Vampire heart is still intact, their Integrity is above 1, and Ephemera is still in their system, they can potentially come back as a Jiang Shi. To do this they must spend 1 Ephemera and roll Intelligence + Manipulation + Supernatural Resistance, if they get a Success they become a Jiang Shi, they convert all of their remaning Ephemera into Essence and start out with 6 Humanity, and Blood Potency of 1 + Vampiric Potency, but if they fail, they can try again. The attempt they can try is equal to their Willpower, or when their Ephemera run out, they also don't suffer Ephemera bleed when they're dead, their Willpower also determine when they will rise and become a Jiang Shi.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","user":"Yumlum","date":".  Rule update 09-21-2024, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T09:04:16-07:00","id":1542368,"title":"","content":"<br /> I highly recommend reading Bloody Dots on Discipline Design <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/280672\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/280672</a><br /> <br /> Overall, I don't see the need to introduce essence as a secondary resource pool for Jiang Shi - after all, vampires usually drink blood to get to life essence to convert that to Vitae, so Jiang Shi could do the same with breath.<br /> <br /> The discipline itself could be something more akin to a &quot;physical&quot; disciplines, it's passive effect granting you the ability to inflict WP damage to gain Vitae (and then deal damage without having to bite to drain the person), while it's actives could enable the vampire to jump/float, and maybe even &quot;dodge&quot; attacks by becoming insubstantial for a turn (Up to dots of the discipline / scene ),<br /> <br /> This would also maintain them having at least 1 physical like discipline in their loadout <br /> <br /> and then weather control could go into the sorcery itself.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 09-18-2024, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T09:18:27-07:00","id":1542369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1542367-jiang-shi-unique-discipline-bloodlines-and-covenant?p=1542368#post1542368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I highly recommend reading Bloody Dots on Discipline Design <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/280672\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/280672</a><br /> <br /> Overall, I don't see the need to introduce essence as a secondary resource pool for Jiang Shi - after all, vampires usually drink blood to get to life essence to convert that to Vitae, so Jiang Shi could do the same with breath.<br /> <br /> The discipline itself could be something more akin to a &quot;physical&quot; disciplines, it's passive effect granting you the ability to inflict WP damage to gain Vitae (and then deal damage without having to bite to drain the person), while it's actives could enable the vampire to jump/float, and maybe even &quot;dodge&quot; attacks by becoming insubstantial for a turn (Up to dots of the discipline / scene ),<br /> <br /> This would also maintain them having at least 1 physical like discipline in their loadout<br /> <br /> and then weather control could go into the sorcery itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was originally the idea I have for them, but then I notice that their Discipline match up with the Kuei-Jin 3 Shintai, with Smoke Shintai being Obfuscate, Beast Shintai being Animalism, and Storm Shintai being Celerity, but I found that Celerity have the weakest tie to the Shintai, so that why I decide to replace it with a unique Discipline, that still have some trace of Celerity, while being it own thing. <br /> <br /> I think Jiang Shi having a secondary resource pool make sense, because they're a strange clan, their embrace need the blood of a pure human (whatever that mean) and they can also teleport to their graves by spending a Willpower, and have undefine ritual for changing grave. And this play to their Clan Bane being the Ephemeral Curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T09:37:45-07:00","id":1542371,"title":"","content":"Sure, you can have them as different. <br /> But what is the difference? <br /> <br /> Since vampires are not after blood, but after life energy, which they draw via blood. <br /> <br /> Jiang Shi draw life energy via breath. Why is this life energy converted to POWER by this vampire not able to power their usual disciplines, but instead gives them a separate pool entirely? The answer could be &quot;different conversion methods&quot;, and it would fit, but I think this complicates things needlessly. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T13:32:20-07:00","id":1542390,"title":"","content":"Since I saw a mention to Kuei-Jin, if the separate pool of essence is to create a sense of similarity, sure, go for it, but this ramps up too much the cost of the later levels and makies a player have to be more considerate with his attributes at Character Creation. It does not provide good uses for the Essence that are not just to fuel the Discipline, and also puts some pressure into developing more attributes so he can have a greater pool of essence. Does it allows him to &quot;Chi-bond&quot; ephemeral beings?<br /> <br /> Also good golly, 9 points of fuel to activate a Discipline power isn't a bit... much?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T19:03:17-07:00","id":1542409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1542367-jiang-shi-unique-discipline-bloodlines-and-covenant#post1542367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the Jiang Shi, but it feel like they are there, they don't even have bloodline or unique discipline, even though they're a full clan that still exist within the modern night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither do the Pijavica, Amari, Hypatians, Nhang, Dukhan or Julii - ok, Julii do have some official bloodlines - for that matter. Considering how much stuff one can do out of messing with devotions somehow tied into a proprietary merit or Bane, sometimes i feel unique disciplines are in a weird &quot;outdated but still current&quot; status as a mechanic. Anyway, 6 official examples of other clans with no unique discipline (not to mention making some of the &quot;core signatures&quot; <i>less</i> unique by their mere existence).<br /> <br /> On bloodlines, nothing to stop you from purloining a bunch of already existing ones and rebranding them as branches of the Jiangshi tree - damn, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Norvegi\" target=\"_blank\">these guys</a> with all the dubiousness in their origins as is are pretty much asking for it. In fact, i think there are some not-so stealth references to them and the Sons of Phobos both in the Jiang Shi clan write up for Requiem 2nd ed, if memory tricks me not.<br /> <br /> Now speaking of the Jiang Shi's actual antiquity in that Requiem 2e's text makes it <i>immensely </i>dubious (by intent, might be said) if they would be counted an ancient clan or instead a <b><i>very </i></b>new clan <i>evolving in modern nights</i> from ancient non-kindred wicked dead monstrosities. And that without going into the uncannily deep rabbit hole of the Jiangshi many parallels and similarities to the Mekhet and even more so to odd atavisms/clan variants like the Hollow Mekhet or Ayanda in Spilled Blood, what could mean that so are the Jiangshi, depending on one's point of view.<br /> <br /> What shouldn't stop you - personal perspective is key here and such divergences of perspective, both from outside and <b>in character</b> perspectives can result in lots of conflict, doubt, debate, mystery and more. Speaking of weirdness and mechanics to draw from, you might want to look in 1e Mythologies and Night Horrors: Wicked Dead for contrast &amp; comparisons. Your discipline in particular reminded me of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Breath-Drinking\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, among other things.<br /> <br /> Plus, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1415618#post1415618\">a few old ramblings of mine </a>on the subject of less known clans, history, truth, lies &amp; related bits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-19-2024, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T21:55:39-07:00","id":1542413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1542367-jiang-shi-unique-discipline-bloodlines-and-covenant?p=1542371#post1542371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, you can have them as different.<br /> But what is the difference?<br /> <br /> Since vampires are not after blood, but after life energy, which they draw via blood.<br /> <br /> Jiang Shi draw life energy via breath. Why is this life energy converted to POWER by this vampire not able to power their usual disciplines, but instead gives them a separate pool entirely? The answer could be &quot;different conversion methods&quot;, and it would fit, but I think this complicates things needlessly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Jiang Shi Clan have more spirit like quality to them than the other clan, they need Essence to make themselves more rooted in the world, they can convert blood into Essence, but it take more power to do it, than just converting breath it self.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1542367-jiang-shi-unique-discipline-bloodlines-and-covenant?p=1542390#post1542390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Since I saw a mention to Kuei-Jin, if the separate pool of essence is to create a sense of similarity, sure, go for it, but this ramps up too much the cost of the later levels and makies a player have to be more considerate with his attributes at Character Creation. It does not provide good uses for the Essence that are not just to fuel the Discipline, and also puts some pressure into developing more attributes so he can have a greater pool of essence. Does it allows him to &quot;Chi-bond&quot; ephemeral beings?<br /> <br /> Also good golly, 9 points of fuel to activate a Discipline power isn't a bit... much?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Essence also let you not suffer the full effect of the Ephemeral Curse, the Jiang Shi can spend 1 Essence to inflict the (Numb) condition, or 3 Essence to inflict the (Addict) condition to the victim of their feeding. And also without Essence they suffer the (Languid) condition, and if they fall into Torpor this way, they can only be wake up when they get Essence.<br /> <br /> They can bound ephemeral being to their service with their Chi Art, but to get access to it they either must be from a particular bloodline of Jiang Shi, or be a part of The Baise Ba Yue Court.<br /> <br /> Well, you it for a power that can potentially block out the sun, and do untold amount of damage for many scene, so I think 9 point of fuel is a bit too generous, but the chance of getting 5 success is slim enough that I didn't want to make it higher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T23:15:55-07:00","id":1542415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1542367-jiang-shi-unique-discipline-bloodlines-and-covenant?p=1542413#post1542413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you it for a power that can potentially block out the sun, and do untold amount of damage for many scene, so I think 9 point of fuel is a bit too generous, but the chance of getting 5 success is slim enough that I didn't want to make it higher.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires are overwhelmingly nocturnal with mechanics to reinforce it and the Jiang Shi as written are not an exception to this. You could change the Duration to &quot;until sunrise&quot; and it would change very little about the power in practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-19T02:02:09-07:00","id":1542416,"title":"","content":"9 points of fuel is an amount, for which I would expect to do amazingly powerful things. Having the successes scale on what is possible seems a bit weak if anything. <br /> <br /> I should have asked to begin with, but are you looking for feedback or just showing us what you wrote? <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-19T02:22:52-07:00","id":1542418,"title":"","content":"I am looking for feedback.<br /> <br /> You think it should cost less or have it be more powerful?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-19T04:56:44-07:00","id":1542419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1542367-jiang-shi-unique-discipline-bloodlines-and-covenant?p=1542418#post1542418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You think it should cost less or have it be more powerful?</div> </div> </div> </div>Comparing it to other powers that do similar things, there is a Level 3 Theban Sorcery Ritual that blocks the Sun.<br /> It requires the expenditure of a Humanity Dot, and the duration is 10 minutes per remaining Humanity. It can cause a bit of rain as well.<br /> <br /> The 2nd edition works better with Conditions and Tilts. What you are describing is a power that causes enviromental tilts at level 5.<br /> If you want to go this route, there is a specific Common Contracts from changeling(wich in theory have the same power of levels 1, 2 or 3 from a Discipline) that can cause enviromental Tilts aligned with the themes you are trying to portray, it's the Autumn's Fury contract, I suggest you give it a look for some inspiration.<br /> <br /> Either way, IMO powers that block one major vampire weakness(the Sun) should come not at the cost of 9 fuel points, but at the cost of something else, like extense ritual preparation or sacrifices, but this would change the power to be a Ritual, and not a Discipline power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-19T06:30:48-07:00","id":1542423,"title":"","content":"I fully forgotten that Environmental existed.<br /> <br /> Thank for the the suggest, I will look into other gameline for inspiration.<br /> <br /> I think there is element of Discipline that can cross into Ritual, but Discipline are often extension of either the Blood or the Beast, with the Tempest God Body and other God Body Discipline, it's also the extension of Essence, the stuff that make spirit powerful, and can influence reality in direct way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-19T10:02:46-07:00","id":1542432,"title":"","content":"A lot of this feels like it's written with the expectation that most (all) Jiang Shi's will have access to this. What about the ones who will not be ingesting in either of these two disciplines?<br /> Do they work fine without access to these abilities? If these abilities are must haves, then they should be worked into the default Jiang Shi template and not be an <i>optional</i> ability the characters can acquire.<br /> <br /> <br /> as such, I would focus the discipline itself on movement and perhaps weather control. Although, to simplify things, I would probably just focus it on movement and make it in a style of Physical discipline, move weather control to be rituals, and move base template abilities.. to well base template.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T07:04:45-07:00","id":1542479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1542367-jiang-shi-unique-discipline-bloodlines-and-covenant?p=1542413#post1542413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mask of the Thousand Faces</b> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> <b>Target of Success: </b>6<br /> The Jiang Shi creates a mask and become the form of that mask. The Jiang Shi must kill the person he wish to assume form of, and use their skin as ingredient in making of the mask. The form created by this power typically possesses the same height, build, ethnicity, and gender of the victim, but otherwise the power can alter his appearance significantly. The Jiang Shi may choose to make the form particularly alluring, unassuming, or monsterous, granting a +3 bonus to Persuasion and Socialize (for the alluring), Stealth and Subterfuge (for the unassuming) or Intimidation and Brawl (for the monsterous). This power lasts for a month, though the Jiang Shi can end it as an instant action or extend it for another month with a recasting of this Art.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once wrote pretty much this power as a Obfuscate+Getsumei devotion for the Burakumin asian Nosferatu bloodline. Possibly somewhat relevant on account of your interest in tinkering with kindred covenants and lineages in Asia.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of asian kindred, once sketched a clan of my own, where i mixed <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Formosae\" target=\"_blank\">Formosae</a>, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Galloi\" target=\"_blank\">Galloi </a>&amp; <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Aswang\" target=\"_blank\">Aswang</a> (though more precisely an all-female &quot;early edition&quot; variant from the Antagonists bluebook) under a &quot;beauty hiding atrocity&quot; theme, based on Taiwan (because Formosa, duh <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />), with the worship of Cybele (cited by the lore of the first two a as source of their &quot;from grotesque horror to alien beauty&quot; powers and themes) adapted through a cthonic version of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doumu\" target=\"_blank\">Doumu</a> in her place.<br /> <br /> Though i'll be the first to admit i was just improvising from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Izanami\" target=\"_blank\">Izanami </a>more than anything. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1542367-jiang-shi-unique-discipline-bloodlines-and-covenant?p=1542413#post1542413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Jiang Shi Clan have more spirit like quality to them than the other clan, they need Essence to make themselves more rooted in the world, they can convert blood into Essence, but it take more power to do it, than just converting breath it self.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the nitpickery but, imho at least, the idea of wielding of a substance ephemeral like Essence, gathered through the act of breath-drinking to boot, seem to do the opposite of &quot;grounding&quot; the undead as you propose, when compared &amp; contrasted to the physical, visceral, potentially violent act that is the feeding upon blood by a vampire.<br /> <br /> Not opposed to the Jiangshi having powers that let their &quot;foot deeper in the grave&quot; show, but things with Essence seem to be running counter to the supposed motive behind them so far.<br /> <br /> Just my two cents of thought.<br /> <br /> Ah - <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1438855-bloodline-to-clan?p=1472036#post1472036\">one more thing</a> perhaps of some relevance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-21-2024, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T19:40:04-07:00","id":1542500,"title":"","content":"Some questions and thoughts on this:<br /> <br /> 1 - How you explain Essence here, or their need for it, is immaterial. What\u2019s the purpose of this added layer of complexity for the game design?<br /> <br /> 2 - For whatever it matters, \u201ctypical\u201d Jiang-Shi feed only on qi, not on qi AND blood. And qi isn\u2019t Essence. Essence in CoD is a specific substance linked to the Shadow and its Spirit denizens. Qi is an energy/substance related to breathing and fuels normal life, it has zero to do with spirit.<br /> <br /> 3 - As comic as it seems, their rigidity, not their breath-feeding, is their defining feature in both folklore and pop culture. They may be agile, even supernaturally so, but never supple, they\u2019re stiff as dead matter, or even as if in rigor mortis.<br /> <br /> 4 - Jiang-shi that don\u2019t \u201ceat\u201d qi, which isn\u2019t uncommon, eat meat. Again, not blood.<br /> <br /> 5 - Tying their basic survival to a Discipline is a big problem. Disciplines are optional powers, and ones that anyone can theoretically learn on top of that. If you want to keep them needing a qi-like resource, being able to feed should come in their basic package.<br /> <br /> 6 - If you want to keep it as a second resource, get rid of the need, it should only be used to fuel the Discipline that creates it in the first place, or as an optional alternative to uses of Vitae. And if you want to tie it to some stat, tie it to the Discipline level.<br /> <br /> 7 - Wolves don\u2019t have \u201cAlphas\u201d. Drop it, that\u2019s an old and very dangerous misconception that\u2019s used to justify a lot of harmful behavior in real life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T05:19:39-07:00","id":1542544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1542367-jiang-shi-unique-discipline-bloodlines-and-covenant?p=1542500#post1542500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some questions and thoughts on this:<br /> <br /> 1 - How you explain Essence here, or their need for it, is immaterial. What\u2019s the purpose of this added layer of complexity for the game design?<br /> <br /> 2 - For whatever it matters, \u201ctypical\u201d Jiang-Shi feed only on qi, not on qi AND blood. And qi isn\u2019t Essence. Essence in CoD is a specific substance linked to the Shadow and its Spirit denizens. Qi is an energy/substance related to breathing and fuels normal life, it has zero to do with spirit.<br /> <br /> 3 - As comic as it seems, their rigidity, not their breath-feeding, is their defining feature in both folklore and pop culture. They may be agile, even supernaturally so, but never supple, they\u2019re stiff as dead matter, or even as if in rigor mortis.<br /> <br /> 4 - Jiang-shi that don\u2019t \u201ceat\u201d qi, which isn\u2019t uncommon, eat meat. Again, not blood.<br /> <br /> 5 - Tying their basic survival to a Discipline is a big problem. Disciplines are optional powers, and ones that anyone can theoretically learn on top of that. If you want to keep them needing a qi-like resource, being able to feed should come in their basic package.<br /> <br /> 6 - If you want to keep it as a second resource, get rid of the need, it should only be used to fuel the Discipline that creates it in the first place, or as an optional alternative to uses of Vitae. And if you want to tie it to some stat, tie it to the Discipline level.<br /> <br /> 7 - Wolves don\u2019t have \u201cAlphas\u201d. Drop it, that\u2019s an old and very dangerous misconception that\u2019s used to justify a lot of harmful behavior in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>1 - It's because I want them to have more connection to the world of ghost, spirit, and other ephemeral being, other than just their Clan Bane, and a few weird abilities. And also it would explain why their number is so low, other than their embrace being more special, but their embrace in the core rulebook isn't much harder than a normal embrace, they just need to find those people who are &quot;pure&quot;, which I guess mean the Purified, but it wasn't really explain.<br /> <br /> 2 - That true for actual Jiang Shi, but the Jiang Shi vampire aren't actual Jiang Shi, it's a reimagining of the Jiang Shi myth, kind of like the other Supernatural Creature within Chronicle of Darkness. In the official text of Vampire the Requiem, it's said that they have spirit like attribute, and their Bane is even call Ephemeral Curse, all of which fuel by Essence.<br /> <br /> 3 - Jiang Shi in official Vampire the Requiem core rulebook text, have Celerity, and their Clan description doesn't mention anything that would make them rigid. And again, it's a reimagining, not an accurate protray of Jiang Shi from culture.<br /> <br /> 4 - True, but it's a reimagining, and Vampire can't really digest flesh.<br /> <br /> 5 - I change that now.<br /> <br /> 6 - If I tie it to the Discipline level, it would just create more problem that it solve, and it couldn't go beyond 5, which you can go beyond, if you tie it to Resolve. And I want to still make it need, to explain why they're so rare.<br /> <br /> 7 - I change that too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T06:30:29-07:00","id":1542547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1542367-jiang-shi-unique-discipline-bloodlines-and-covenant?p=1542544#post1542544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And also it would explain why their number is so low, other than their embrace being more special, but their embrace in the core rulebook isn't much harder than a normal embrace, they just need to find those people who are &quot;pure&quot;, which I guess mean the Purified, but it wasn't really explain.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Jiang Shi's purity prerequisite is a moral/spiritual one; the reference &quot;somebody who could cast the first stone&quot; in the clan writeup is alluding to the Biblical line &quot;let he who is without sin cast the first stone.&quot; The heart transplant ritual carries over the story from the non-Kindred Jiang Shi writeup in <i>Night Horrors: Wicked Dead</i> describing how the ritual to become a Jiang Shi (which, in Night Horrors, are not a clan and cannot perform the Embrace) requires the heart (the vessel of the higher soul) of a virgin, and the named character who that introductory story revolves around was both a virgin and highly religious. The Strix bane &quot;Plague of Purity&quot; applies its effects from the touch of a human with Integrity of 8 or higher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T15:39:22-07:00","id":1542586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1542367-jiang-shi-unique-discipline-bloodlines-and-covenant?p=1542544#post1542544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jiang Shi in official Vampire the Requiem core rulebook text, have Celerity</div> </div> </div> </div>Not arguing, just to clarify: Celerity does make sense. In many tales and legends the Jiang-Shi have preternatural agility and speed. It\u2019s just that their movements always seem rigid even if quick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T18:01:22-07:00","id":1542597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1542367-jiang-shi-unique-discipline-bloodlines-and-covenant?p=1542586#post1542586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not arguing, just to clarify: Celerity does make sense. In many tales and legends the Jiang-Shi have preternatural agility and speed. It\u2019s just that their movements always seem rigid even if quick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that could now be explain by Jiang Shi who don't have Essence in their system, causing them to gain Languid condition, which make their movement rigid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T20:54:49-07:00","id":1542603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1542367-jiang-shi-unique-discipline-bloodlines-and-covenant?p=1542597#post1542597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that could now be explain by Jiang Shi who don't have Essence in their system, causing them to gain Languid condition, which make their movement rigid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to point out that Languid as an adjective is the <i>diametrical opposite</i> of rigid movements. Just sayin'.<br /> <br /> No offense, but imho it's starting to look like you are <b><i>really</i> </b>deadset into bringing a &quot;essence as alternate magical fuel pool&quot; system into play and everything else are just excuses.<br /> At this point wouldn't you be better of making a homebrew asian clan of your own from scratch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T21:14:55-07:00","id":1542604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1542367-jiang-shi-unique-discipline-bloodlines-and-covenant?p=1542603#post1542603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd like to point out that Languid as an adjective is the <i>diametrical opposite</i> of rigid movements. Just sayin'.<br /> <br /> No offense, but imho it's starting to look like you are <b><i>really</i> </b>deadset into bringing a &quot;essence as alternate magical fuel pool&quot; system into play and everything else are just excuses.<br /> At this point wouldn't you be better of making a homebrew asian clan of your own from scratch?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not my intention, it's just that Essence pool fit with the Jiang Shi as describe within VtR 2e core rulebook, I'm not making excuse, it just seem perfect for Jiang Shi in my eye. And why would I make another asian clan, when the one with an Asian name, that exist within the Core Rulebook of Second Edition, exist and doesn't have much information to give them a more solid identity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T03:09:36-07:00","id":1542619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1542367-jiang-shi-unique-discipline-bloodlines-and-covenant?p=1542604#post1542604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is not my intention, it's just that Essence pool fit with the Jiang Shi as describe within VtR 2e core rulebook, I'm not making excuse, it just seem perfect for Jiang Shi in my eye. And why would I make another asian clan, when the one with an Asian name, that exist within the Core Rulebook of Second Edition, exist and doesn't have much information to give them a more solid identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me it feels a bit shoehorned in and unnecessary. I like some ideas here, but if I'll ever use Jiang Shi I'll be homebrewing my own version. <br /> <br /> Inclusion of Essence overcomplicated this a lot. <br /> <br /> I would consider creating a base Jiang Shi clan, and then have a blood line introduce essence for itself. <br /> <br /> For a base clan there's too many things to juggle here, IMO. <br /> <br /> From game design perspective it's overcomplicated. <br /> <br /> Simplify for base clan, keep essentials. Add bloodlines which add such complications like a whole new pool of resources (essence).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T05:02:16-07:00","id":1542622,"title":"","content":"Another question: why does the base clan give them extra abilities to spend the said essence? if you're hellbent on keeping Essence in, then there's no need for them to have 2 abilities built into where they can spend essence. Really, I'd even say 1 is too much - if Essence is essential for them, then at the base clan, their Bane/drawback should make them require it (and spend as is), and then give them ability to gather it (drain it from humans).<br /> <br /> In this case, move Numb and Addicted abilities into In-Clan merits, which characters can choose to have. Notice how other base clans have their basic themes expressed through the bane and disciplines and then In-Clan abilities are merits (Dream Visions, Kiss of Succcubus, etc etc). I think same should apply here. Base Clan should have the bare minimum number of abilities and things to make it work.<br /> <br /> if for your clan it is Essence (which I think it sohuldn't be, but) - then that's all there should be. Actually all of it could be their Clan Bane: &quot;Every night you don't sleep in your grave lose a point of Essence, or suffer 1 aggravated damage. When gaining Vitae, you can instead gain Essence and you can store maximum of Resolve of Essence.&quot;.<br /> <br /> Then have a 1 dot merit, &quot;Drinker of Essence&quot; which allows you to gather it via breath and not bite. Then another merit which allows you to spend essence to inflict Numb or Addicted.<br /> <br /> The Discipline should step away from essence and it's use (although you could, if you really wanted to, have the discipline say that &quot;characters with available Essence can spend it instead of Vitae costs associated with the Discipline&quot;. Have the Discipline be in Vitae costs and focused on air powers (given that it's replacing celerity, I'd make it a Physical like ability).<br /> This is also potentially important because other vampires might want to learn this Discipline and they should be able to power it with Vitae.<br /> <br /> Other abilities in what you currently have could become Devotions (This Discipline + Animalism to control the weather, perhaps??)<br /> <br /> This in total would clean up the design of the Clan to make it more in line with other Clans, while keeping it's themes and access to the list of abilities you wish to have.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 09-25-2024, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T06:45:29-07:00","id":1542627,"title":"","content":"Thank you for all the suggestion <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar294_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"294\" data-vbnamecard=\"294\">Griautis</a>, I will incorporate some element of your suggestion into my homebrew as soon as I can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T19:24:22-07:00","id":1542657,"title":"","content":"After giving it some thought, I'd like to add that if you want to connect them to Ghosts, Spirits and other ephemerals, what you need is to give them access to abilities that interact with Twilight.<br /> <br /> Essence by itself, while the common fuel of those entities, isn\u2019t neither required nor sufficient. It just makes them nominally use the same substance.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also still deeply out of context to drain Essence from humans. Humans don\u2019t have Essence to be drained. And while we can generate it, everything else also can and does, even inanimate objects. It is out of touch with what Essence is in the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T20:37:55-07:00","id":1542661,"title":"","content":"I'd point out that the Strix, even in their incorporeal shadow forms that steal the breath of the living, use Vitae. If you're talking about a numinous spark of life being stolen from the living and consumed for occult power, that's Vitae, not Essence. Blood is one vessel through which Vitae can be stolen and retained, but it isn't necessary. Essence in CofD isn't the life-force coursing through the world. It's a phantasmagoric ephemera-stuff harnessed by outsiders too distant in nature to easily touch the material world.<br /> <br /> Drop Essence as a separate resource, and if you want Jiang Shi feeding to be more otherworldly, just give them the ability to learn to steal breath without physically touching their victim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T02:12:24-07:00","id":1542672,"title":"","content":"I could also recommend googling for the meaning of the word &quot;Vitae&quot;. And &quot;Essence&quot;. While the game uses them in different meanings, they're still somewhat derived of the wider meaning. <br /> <br /> OP, what does using Essence here give you exactly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T02:49:43-07:00","id":1542674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1542367-jiang-shi-unique-discipline-bloodlines-and-covenant?p=1542672#post1542672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could also recommend googling for the meaning of the word &quot;Vitae&quot;. And &quot;Essence&quot;. While the game uses them in different meanings, they're still somewhat derived of the wider meaning.<br /> <br /> OP, what does using Essence here give you exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's my vision for what the Jiang Shi is like. And I think Essence make them closer to Ephemeral being.<br /> <br /> I feel like I heard the explanation for Essence multiple time, and each one is different, so can anyone tell me what Essence really is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T03:26:43-07:00","id":1542675,"title":"","content":"Corebook definition:<br /> Essence: A combination of food, oxygen, and wealth, Essence fuels ephemeral entities\u2019 powers, sustains their insubstantial bodies, and allows them to continue existing.<br /> <br /> Having said that, it's kinda vague, as the empheral entities which use this resource all colour/use essence of colours/flavours which makes sense to them.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd like you to also consider the &quot;feel&quot; of playing a Jiang-Shi. Having a second pool of resources to juggle increases mechanical complexity, but does it actually _feel_ different. When telling the stories, or writing these stories up, how is it different when Jiang-Shi spends Vitae vs Essence? it doesn't really, because to Jiang-Shi both are &quot;energetic power resource I use to fuel abilities (or maintain my existence).<br /> <br /> The feel of being Ephemeral like entity is not going to come from the resource pool they have (or unnecessary complications of it). Why does it have to juggle two resources? Why not just have them use Essence for all things and not use Vitae at all then?<br /> <br /> That feel comes from abilities. Abilities that can be fully fueled by Vitae.<br /> <br /> What I mean by above is, here's a story example:<br /> &quot;The Scary Jiang-Shi vampire Su Shan slowly floats towards you. As you unload your bullets into it's body, and those bullets just go right through them and smash the vase behind Su Shan's smile widens. 'You can't harm the untouchable'. He says as his form floats ever closer to you, then it snaps and vanishes appearing mear inches away from your face. You can see him take a deep breath and you can't help but feel your own life be sucked out through your nostrils and mouth. Your lungs clench up trying to hold on to air, but sip by sip Su Shan steals your life force&quot;.<br /> <br /> So did Su Shan use Vitae or Essence for the above? I don't see why it wouldn't be Vitae And yet, it gets to have empheral abilities, sucking of air.<br /> And if the answer to the above is &quot;essence&quot;. then I'd say - well why would he ever use Vitae, and so I'd just make the entire pool of it's resources be just Essence. Having to juggle two separate resources does not actually add to the feel or flavor - it's just mechanical complication visible to the OOC entities (players, ST).<br /> <br /> Of note, something to consider is the &quot;source&quot; of each resource. Vitae is life drained from mortals. Essence is.. an empheral energy which appears when certain things/actions create it. If you truly wanna go Essence way - then you should look more at the rules of Essence, and so it's not really a &quot;drainable&quot; resource from Mortals. At base of it! Obviously, you can have abilities which convert the two. I think this is at the core of some of the disagreements proposed by other posters in the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 09-26-2024, 07:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T04:06:10-07:00","id":1542677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1542367-jiang-shi-unique-discipline-bloodlines-and-covenant?p=1542674#post1542674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like I heard the explanation for Essence multiple time, and each one is different, so can anyone tell me what Essence really is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spiritual energy. Exactly what this means differs depending on the type of ephemeral entity we're talking about. For spirits (which I believe is the type relevant for this topic) Essence is the energy that's derived from material sources they happen to resonate with (hence why the associated Condition is called Resonant).<br /> Someone being angry generates anger Essence for anger/rage spirits to consume. A lit fireplace generates fire Essence for fire spirits to consume. A stone generates stone Essence for stone spirits. (The intensity of the source does influence how much Essence is generated, but this isn't really modelled by the rules for how spirits gain Essence. Also, once Essence enters the spiritual ecology, it can be passed around in various ways.)<br /> An important part of all of this is that Essence is <i>typed</i>, i.e. anger Essence is distinct from fire Essence which is distinct from stone Essence.<br /> Another important part of all of this is that while everything generates Essence, nothing <i>contains</i> Essence. This is why some people have opposed the idea that your Jiang-Shi would be able to suck out Essence from humans. There's just no Essence to be had. This is also why people think Essence is a poor fit for qi. The concept of qi much more closely aligns with Vitae (especially the breath kind that Strix uses) since that's actually found within humans.<br /> Also, Essence, while generated in our world, is highly tied to the spirit world, meaning it's really not grounding the Jiang-Shi in the world of the living.<br /> <br /> Now there <b>is</b> a very prominent example of Essence being gained by directly <b>eating</b> a human: Werewolves. They can also do it on wolves. However, it should be noted that werewolves <b>are</b> partly spirits, and merely mix their spiritual nature (drawing Essence from what they resonate with) and their physical nature (physically consuming things for nourishment). This only works because humans and wolves are Resonant for werewolves.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also want to add to the sentiment that adding Essence as a separate fuel stat to track is adding needless complexity just from a pure gameplay perspective. Such things are better of as Bloodline Gifts, where there's a conscious buy-in to the new mechanics.<br /> Additionally, Clans have a few things that differentiate them from each other, from favoured Attributes to in-Clan Disciplines to Clan Banes. Of these, Clan Banes are the only ones that add unique rules to the individual Clans. Now, Clan Banes can be complex, but they are meant as a <i>drawback</i>. Adding extra rules separates them <i>away</i> from the other Clans, which is what their official write-up already does by introducing special rules for Embraces and their teleportation power.<br /> Lastly, having a Discipline that requires access to Essence makes it <i>impossible</i> to use for other Clans. (I also think Celerity is a great fit for Jiang-Shi based on their folklore, so it's certainly not the one I'd replace anyway.)<br /> <br /> Now, having extra rules and even a truly unique Discipline are not necessarily bad things. It really depends on what your goal with them is. But I do get the feeling that you're trying to make them more in-line with the regular Clans and present them as a player option, which these additions runs counter for the above mentioned reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T16:00:31-07:00","id":1542717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1542367-jiang-shi-unique-discipline-bloodlines-and-covenant?p=1542674#post1542674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like I heard the explanation for Essence multiple time, and each one is different, so can anyone tell me what Essence really is?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> did a great job explaining, I'll <b>try</b> to add a more succint view.<br /> <br /> Essence is the \u201cephemeral reflection\u201d of a material thing. Aside from a few complications, the gist of it is that each \u201cthing\u201d that exists, be it a living organism, object, landscape, emotion, abstraction, action or whatever, generates Essence while it exists. Except humans, they don\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Nothing material <b>contains</b> Essence, though. It is exclusively an ephemeral thing. As soon as it is generated it is either consumed by an ephemeral entity, or it goes to an otherworld and sits there doing nothing. Most of it goes to the Shadow, memory-generated Essence goes to the Underworld. The God-Machine produces the Essence Angels consume<br /> <br /> What distinguishes Essence from other resources is that Ephemeral entities can exchange it between themselves. That\u2019s it. Having Essence only will mean anything if you picture the Jiang-Shi taking part in spiritual economy. But I do think that really adds too much complications to the base clan, and it would still not come from human breath. It wouldn't by itself interact with them, either.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s unknown why humans do not generate \u201cHuman Essence\u201d. Their emotions, actions and abstract concepts do generate Essence as usual (as do those of any sentient being), and Werewolves can generate Essence from the act of eating humans, but there\u2019s no actual \u201cEssence of Human\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T18:19:53-07:00","id":1542729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1542367-jiang-shi-unique-discipline-bloodlines-and-covenant?p=1542717#post1542717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essence is the \u201cephemeral reflection\u201d of a material thing. Aside from a few complications, the gist of it is that each \u201cthing\u201d that exists, be it a living organism, object, landscape, emotion, abstraction, action or whatever, generates Essence while it exists. Except humans, they don\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Nothing material <b>contains</b> Essence, though. It is exclusively an ephemeral thing. As soon as it is generated it is either consumed by an ephemeral entity, or it goes to an otherworld and sits there doing nothing. Most of it goes to the Shadow, memory-generated Essence goes to the Underworld. The God-Machine produces the Essence Angels consume<br /> <br /> What distinguishes Essence from other resources is that Ephemeral entities can exchange it between themselves. That\u2019s it. Having Essence only will mean anything if you picture the Jiang-Shi taking part in spiritual economy. But I do think that really adds too much complications to the base clan, and it would still not come from human breath. It wouldn't by itself interact with them, either.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s unknown why humans do not generate \u201cHuman Essence\u201d. Their emotions, actions and abstract concepts do generate Essence as usual (as do those of any sentient being), and Werewolves can generate Essence from the act of eating humans, but there\u2019s no actual \u201cEssence of Human\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking a different, lengthier tack on this to also steer toward the more salient ephemeral being relevant to the Jiang Shi:<br /> <br /> Humans generate a great deal of Essence \u2014 one of the reasons they cause so much trouble with the effects they have on the spiritual ecosystem through their actions \u2014 but what they don't generate directly is <i>spirits of themselves and related beings</i>. That distinction instead belongs to <i>ghosts</i>, which, while not being exclusively of human things, privileges human Integrity and its erosion in determining the relative strength of ghosts formed by or in relation to human trauma including but not limited to death.<br /> <br /> The bodies of spirits and ghosts are composed of different varieties of ephemera; they store Essence, and the Essence generated by the resonance of a phenomenon tends to be absorbed by the ephemeral body of its attending spirit, but it's not so much that Essence is the reflection of a thing as it is that the ephemeral reflections of things are sustained by Essence \u2014 Essence ensures that a spirit of ice remains cold by being the cold that reifies it as a spirit of ice.<br /> <br /> Notably, spirits and ghosts are both identified in parts of the books that deal with ancient Egyptian soul anatomy (not just from Mummy) with the Ka, a.k.a. the Essence of the fivefold soul, which distinguishes a living being from a dead one and which the metaphysics primer in the Mekhet clanbook describes as the Soul of Sustenance because it's the part of you that eats and makes sure you survive.<br /> <br /> Spirits and ghosts both live up to the role of the Ka by absorbing Essence from things that sustain them (their originating phenomena for spirits, the Anchors relating to their former life and death for ghosts) on a drip feed and by consumption of other spirits of appropriate resonance for spirits and of other ghosts for ghosts who can't rely on living people remembering them as they once were. Consumption can hypothetically be a little abstract for spirits, because the flesh and blood of a big box supermarket and money, however metaphorically represented, are probably going to bear little resemblance to that of living creatures, but the process is still visceral; it's doubly so for ghosts, as ectophagia of the ghost of a creature requires eating ephemeral organs and other innards (and objects aren't much better, since Castoffs retain their Durability and most ghosts don't have teeth that can overcome that without undergoing some transformations).<br /> <br /> Essence is, broadly, the energy of the living world \u2014 out in material-adjacent reality, ghosts and spirits are geographically constrained by its different flavors not being omnipresent and the God-Machine engineers Infrastructure into patterns that its angels can run on in lieu of material sacrifices (burning the Essence like fuel to produce Aetheric reactions rather than using it to sustain themselves like food for a living creature), while the goetia that live inside of the souls of humanity and the world get it for free just by existing where they do. Werewolves use Essence instead of something else because they are part of the Essential ecosystem of the Shadow, and as human-passing fleshy entities their methods for gaining Essence are as visceral as one would expect from a desperate ghost or a spirit of a humanoid creature. You have a supernatural being run on Essence to make a statement about its relationship as part of the world through the means by which it gets that Essence. (This is, if I'm not mistaken, why Yumlum talked about wanting to have the Jiang Shi run on Essence to make them more rooted in the world.)<br /> <br /> A possible explanation for why there are no spirits of humanity \u2014 if one takes the Mekhet clanbook's metaphysics primer and the above associations with the Ka as true-enough \u2014 is that when the human Ka is set free after death and is given to wander from lack of appropriate mourning rites, it takes the shadow of the deceased, i.e. their image and representation in the world, which is why the Ka of the Hollow Mekhet is modeled as a ghost, albeit one given to a slightly unusual Ban around its manifestations; in the soul anatomy used by Chronicles, shadows, ghosts, and the Ka of the Hollow Mekhet all fall under the sway of the part of Awakened magic most readily practiced by the Path whose symbolism deals with the shadow as part of the soul. Before death, a whole human soul exists in a metaphysical state largely walled off from spiritual unity with the rest of the world (there's a great big rock in the way of the meditative path from the collective unconscious to the soul of the universe, where everything communicates in the language of hunger and ecstatic pain, and the only way to cross that divide without mystical practices is to be one of the wild folk who don't have the same sort of interface with the inner realms as normal people, like werewolves or Beasts). With the Ka bound within the body and mind before death and held to the shadows after death, the human reflection lacks in direct conversation with the spirit world without specialized transformations like those the Purified undergo.<br /> <br /> The Jiang Shi are not spirit-vampires, but ghost-adjacent vampires. Their ability to teleport to their &quot;grave&quot; is a carryover from them literally having Anchors like a ghost in their 1e mechanics. They are notably different from ghosts in not having access to fuel sources that aren't harvested by their own activities, which means the involvement of the living in the process of Jiang Shi sustenance would be limited to Being Consumed, but as a Type Of Vampire they do not have the benefits of an ephemeral constitution nor the innate vitality of a werewolf to justify having them work like things that use Essence, which means that giving them an Essence pool in place of Vitae would only serve about the same function as Hunter modeling every fuel-using monster as harvesting or generating Willpower (i.e. for simplicity's sake in a game where Essence is already relevant and Vitae is not), and giving them an Essence pool <i>in addition to</i> a Vitae pool is, as mentioned, either more appropriate to a further refined branch of the clan (a la some bloodline gifts, like the Dragolescu's Essentiaphagia using Ectoplasm as a resource) or gilding the lily when the Strix are right there in the corebook harvesting Vitae through the medium of breath (and potentially other weirder methods courtesy of variations on the Soul Bite Dread Power).<br /> <br /> Unless the idea is that the Jiang Shi are using Essence in the same way as angels do \u2014 fungibly and without regard for its source and tenor \u2014 the fact that they are <i>vampires</i> means they do not have the luxury of being treated like a part of the world that naturally belongs where it is. Circle rhetoric and deliberate written ambiguity on the distinction between the natural and the supernatural aside, vampirism is the stuff of curses and traceable lines of descent (however long or short) rather than something that can be taken for granted, and the Phantoms aren't stated not to have a Predatory Aura that impresses itself on their Havens and Feeding Grounds like the rest of the Kindred; they may exert a lighter touch on the world, but their Vitae still spends the same, and the Strix's breath-drinking demonstrates that limitations on what you can do with Vitae are as much about the medium as the energy itself.<br /> <br /> Notably, ghosts are not often about flashy powers like tossing lightning around or centering storms on themselves without having a source of power beyond simple Essence \u2014 the power that comes with higher Rank as a ghost either taps into another magical framework like Utterances or Supernal magic or comes at the cost of drinking from the Rivers of the Underworld or wearing the remnants of those that did, the latter of which entails &quot;becoming more rooted in the world&quot; in the sense of aligning oneself with the universal hunger of death and entropy. Most of Vampire's idiom of undead power outside of powerful ritual magic is relatively subtle and mundane in presentation \u2014 uncanny physical attributes, psychosocial manipulation, rarefied senses and twists of fate \u2014 in keeping with the game being concerned in no small part with keeping the Masquerade on a personal level.<br /> <br /> The Kindred are not designed to be high-energy display pieces when they burn mechanically-tracked amounts of energy just to get up in the evening, and that combined with the Phantoms in particular having a smaller fingerprint on the world makes filtering the energy energy most commonly used by beings that are more invisible and geographically constrained than them to zap things with thunderbolts or summon a tornado feel extremely weird even without getting into the assumption that one needs to take energy in a format that isn't intrinsically stolen to connect a creature to the world that already steals life to remain active in the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}